    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for 2026-07-21 is anchored by **Bryce Harper**, who leads our starting nine with a 70.17 efficiency score. **Bryce Harper** draws a favorable matchup against Wrobleski, and with favorable wind conditions blowing out, he is primed to capitalize on his elite 0.386 xwOBA. **Taylor Ward** follows closely with a 66.63 score, benefiting significantly from his promotion to the leadoff spot and a strong platoon edge against a lefty. While **Gleyber Torres** holds a strong 64.55 score due to his position in the #2 hole and a platoon advantage over Peterson, his status is tempered by a 41% rain risk\u2014a situation we are monitoring closely. Similarly, **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.63) is a high-upside play today; he is taking full advantage of a weak matchup against Avila, where the SP\u2019s high 4.96 xERA creates a perfect storm for our hitters.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's roster was excluding **Lawrence Butler** from the starting outfield. Despite a base projection of 54.42, **Lawrence Butler** was edged out because of the platoon disadvantage against Kohl Drake and his presumed spot at the bottom of the order, which the optimizer penalized relative to the higher-upside profiles of **Gavin Sheets** and **Drew Gilbert**. Elsewhere, **Masyn Winn** remains a vital inclusion; while his score of 58.97 is marginal, his elite speed is prioritized in our strategy, and he faces a favorable 4.62 xERA opponent who historically permits a high rate of stolen base attempts. We are operating with caution regarding **Cal Raleigh** and **Geraldo Perdomo**, both of whom are currently awaiting official lineup confirmation; should **Cal Raleigh** slide down from the expected #4 spot, his efficiency score\u2014already slightly suppressed by a tough matchup against Chase Burns\u2014could warrant further scrutiny before first pitch.",
